{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeStokesEigenvalues"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_closed_form_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_closed_form_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L184-L194","doc":"**τ is bar-even (the cosh-like invariance).** The conditional closed form\n`τ(q) = 3(3q⁴+8q²+3)/(4q(q+1)²)` is invariant under `q ↦ q⁻¹`: `τ(q⁻¹) = τ(q)`. Because `τ`\nfactors through the **even** eigenvalue gap (`tau_in_stokes_eigenvalue_gap`), it inherits the\nbar-evenness of `cosh ξ` — the binding trace cannot see the bar-odd `sinh` direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.curvature_coeff_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.curvature_coeff_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L174-L182","doc":"**Bar-odd (sinh) partner of the eigenvalue gap.** The linear coefficient `q − q⁻¹` of the monodromy quadratic\nflips sign under the Hecke bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`: `q⁻¹ − (q⁻¹)⁻¹ = −(q − q⁻¹)`. Contrast\n`QOU.Mass.HeckeStokes.quantum_dim_bar_even` (the gap `[2]_q`, bar-**even**, cosh). The two\ncombinations are the `sinh`/`cosh` of `ξ = log q` under `ξ ↦ −ξ`. (A pure bar-involution\nidentity — its generic-field partner `quantum_dim_bar_even` lives in `HeckeStokesEigenvalues`;\nhere it is stated over the file's archimedean ring `ℝ`, no ordering needed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_in_stokes_eigenvalue_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_in_stokes_eigenvalue_gap","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L135-L156","doc":"**τ in the non-abelian-Stokes eigenvalue-gap form.** The same conditional τ, written in\nthe eigenvalue gap `b = λ₊ − λ₋ = q − (−q⁻¹) = [2]_q` (`quantum_dim_is_eigenvalue_gap`):\n\n  `τ = 3(3b² + 2) / (4(b + 2))`,\n\nmatching `QOU.Mass.TauQuantumIntegerForm` (`τ = 3(3[2]² + 2)/(4([2]+2))`). This is the\nna-Stokes utilisation made fully explicit: the binding trace is a rational function of the\nHecke/Stokes eigenvalue gap, hence bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_conditional_on_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tau_conditional_on_keystone","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L111-L133","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `conj:sw-prolongation-period-eq-mean-qdim`, #1765).**\nGiven the keystone (period = mean quantum dimension) at the three binding anchors and the\nunconditionally-proved selection-rule values\n`lw(1) = 1`, `lw(2) = (q+1)²/(3q)`, `lw(3) = (3q²+4+3q⁻²)/4`, the depth-2 SL₂ binding trace\nassembles to the **bar-even** closed form\n\n  `τ = 3(3q⁴ + 8q² + 3) / (4q(q+1)²)`.\n\nOnly `ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim` is conjectural; the assembly is sorry-free real\nalgebra. (The `n ≤ 4` effective reading — see the file docstring / PR #2795.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.lw2_eq_two_plus_stokes_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.lw2_eq_two_plus_stokes_gap","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**The `c = 2` selection-rule anchor in the non-abelian-Stokes eigenvalue gap.**\n`lw(2) = (q+1)²/(3q) = (2 + [2]_q)/3`, where `[2]_q = λ₊ − λ₋ = q − (−q⁻¹)` is the gap\nbetween the two Stokes/Hecke eigenvalues (`quantum_dim_is_eigenvalue_gap`). This exhibits\nthe proton-channel anchor that feeds τ as `(2 + eigenvalue-gap)/3`, a direct na-Stokes datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tauOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.tauOf","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L95-L98","doc":"The **depth-2 SL₂ binding trace** `τ = (a_D^(2) + a_D^(4)) / a_D^(3)`, the trace of the\ntransfer matrix `R(q,x) = x² − τ x + 1` fit to the three binding anchors `n = 2, 3, 4`\n(`sl2-prolongation-recurrence`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim.keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim.keystone","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L93-L93","doc":"#1765: the `n`-jet Seiberg–Witten period equals the mean quantum dimension `lw(n−1)`,\ni.e. `aD (c+1) = lw c`. This is the non-abelian-Stokes holonomy → Markov-trace →\n`Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` → mean-quantum-dimension bridge, asserted to hold as an equality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NaStokesKeystone.ProlongationPeriodMeanQuantumDim","kind":"class","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NaStokesKeystone.lean#L77-L93","doc":"**The prolongation-period keystone — `conj:sw-prolongation-period-eq-mean-qdim` (#1765),\naxiomatised as a §3b conjecture class.**\n\n`aD n` is the `n`-th jet-prolongation period `a_D^(n) = ∮_{S_c} λ_SW^(n)` of the\nSeiberg–Witten differential; `lw c` is the selection-rule mean quantum dimension\n`(1/(c+1)) Σ_{λ⊢c+1} dim_q V_λ`. The conjecture asserts the period equals the\nnon-abelian-Stokes / Markov-trace average `lw` at every level:\n\n  `a_D^(n) = lw(n−1)`   i.e.   `aD (c+1) = lw c`.\n\nThis `sorry`-free class is the *only* unproved input of the conditional results below; an\ninstance is the geometric content (step 1→4 of the docstring bridge), not a missing proof. ","signatureChunk":0}]}